Package: diykvm
Version: 0.4.1
Architecture: all
Maintainer: Usama Masood <mirzaon@gmail.com>
Depends: python3 (>= 3.9), python3-venv, python3-pip, ustreamer, dosfstools, gdisk, util-linux, mount, libjpeg62-turbo, gpiod, raspi-gpio
Recommends: socat
Section: admin
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://github.com/n3rd-bugs/diykvm
Description: DIY KVM-over-IP for Raspberry Pi
 Browser-based KVM-over-IP. The Raspberry Pi presents itself to a target
 machine as a USB keyboard, mouse and mass-storage (EFI boot) device, captures
 the target's HDMI through a USB capture dongle, and serves a web UI to control
 input, manage the virtual drive and reach a serial console.
 .
 LAN-only, with session-cookie and API-key authentication. Settings live in
 /etc/kvm/kvm.conf. The Python dependencies are installed into a virtualenv at
 /opt/kvm/venv on first configure.
